WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.440
13,000 Storks nested yearly on Turkish platforms that then raised rural storm outages. This

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:12.120
is unintended consequences, episode 186. In 2009, ADM Electric began mounting special

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:17.660
life platforms on distribution poles in Soke, Iden, to give white Storks safe nesting

00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:22.200
sites away from live conductors. The measure spread to other distribution companies,

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:26.780
and by the 10th year of the program, covered Iden, Denizli, and Mula.

00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:33.185
Angin Ozturk, Environment and Urbanization General Director in Edirna Province, described

00:00:33.185 --> 00:00:36.245
the problem officials saw in villages along Saros Bay.

00:00:37.005 --> 00:00:41.825
Storks returning each spring built Ness directly on cross arms and insulators, where their

00:00:41.825 --> 00:00:44.545
wings or nesting material touched energized parts.

00:00:45.125 --> 00:00:50.005
In November 2020, the provincial directorate of Environment and Urbanization began fitting

00:00:50.005 --> 00:00:54.965
portable nesting platforms on poles together with teams from the local electricity distribution

00:00:54.965 --> 00:00:55.525
company.

00:00:55.525 --> 00:01:00.605
The stated goals were to stop birds from being caught in electrical current, to cut the

00:01:00.605 --> 00:01:04.985
number of malfunctions on rural lines, and to let repair crews work more efficiently

00:01:04.985 --> 00:01:06.185
when faults did occur.

00:01:06.865 --> 00:01:11.985
At the time, the region was known to host about 50,000 migratory birds, so keeping nests

00:01:11.985 --> 00:01:16.565
off live equipment looked like a straightforward way to protect both wildlife and supply

00:01:16.565 --> 00:01:17.125
reliability.

00:01:17.965 --> 00:01:22.985
ADM Electric had already given that 2009 effort the name, a new home for Storks.

00:01:22.985 --> 00:01:28.265
Place platforms on poles in western Turkey and later reported that the Ministry of Energy

00:01:28.265 --> 00:01:32.085
and Natural Resources had asked other distributors to copy the approach.

00:01:32.705 --> 00:01:37.525
Officials treated the platforms as an accommodation that worked with the birds known habit of returning

00:01:37.525 --> 00:01:42.065
to the same site each year, rather than an attempt to remove poles from the landscape.

00:01:42.936 --> 00:01:47.736
By 2020, the Adirna teams had installed the first portable nests on poles in protected

00:01:47.736 --> 00:01:48.616
breeding areas.

00:01:48.616 --> 00:01:54.996
In the Thrace region, Tredash, the distribution company owned by IC Holding, began its own

00:01:54.996 --> 00:02:02.316
platform program around the same period, and by the mid-2020s had placed 1196 platforms

00:02:02.316 --> 00:02:05.656
along its lines, while also adding conductor insulation.

00:02:06.356 --> 00:02:11.516
ADM Electric and its affiliate GDZ Electric continued annual pre-migration maintenance

00:02:11.516 --> 00:02:17.416
on platforms in Iden, Denizli and Mula, cleaning debris and adding insulation near nests.

00:02:17.416 --> 00:02:22.776
Those companies reported fewer emergency callouts for NESTs that had previously shorted lines.

00:02:23.196 --> 00:02:28.096
National media gave the work positive coverage and framed it as an example of utility and

00:02:28.096 --> 00:02:29.136
nature cooperation.

00:02:29.816 --> 00:02:34.716
Partnerships formed with Trakia University and Ega University for monitoring, and the

00:02:34.716 --> 00:02:38.176
Ministry of Energy circulated the ADM model to other operators.

00:02:39.167 --> 00:02:44.107
Once many Storks used the new platforms, NEST density on individual poles rose sharply

00:02:44.107 --> 00:02:49.407
Because each platform offered a stable, elevated site that several pairs sometimes adopted,

00:02:49.847 --> 00:02:51.847
or that successive seasons enlarged.

00:02:52.327 --> 00:02:58.547
T-Pav's October 2026 policy note on Storks, Power Lines and Fire Risk observed that these

00:02:58.547 --> 00:03:03.447
concentrated nests increased the mass and wind load on single structures, so that during

00:03:03.447 --> 00:03:09.187
storms a nest could shift, drop wet material onto conductors below, or cause flashovers

00:03:09.187 --> 00:03:11.987
that earlier scattered nests had been less likely to produce.

00:03:11.987 --> 00:03:16.907
The same note recorded that bird-related contact remained a leading cause of faults

00:03:16.907 --> 00:03:23.107
on Turkish high-voltage lines, with one technical study counting 2,645 such events

00:03:23.107 --> 00:03:28.327
between 2019 and 2024, most attributed to migrating white storks.

00:03:28.687 --> 00:03:33.647
Because platforms kept birds on the network rather than moving them elsewhere, the electrocution

00:03:33.647 --> 00:03:37.767
risk moved from the cross-arm to the edge of the platform, or to neighboring equipment

00:03:37.767 --> 00:03:39.107
when fledglings fluttered.

00:03:39.107 --> 00:03:44.247
Rural customers served by lighter distribution lines experience more frequent and longer

00:03:44.247 --> 00:03:49.147
outages when a single large nest faulted a pole that now carried several nests instead

00:03:49.147 --> 00:03:49.667
of one.

00:03:50.287 --> 00:03:55.147
Treda-Data later showed that insulation and platforms together reduced deaths at monitored

00:03:55.147 --> 00:04:00.227
eagle nests, yet the density effect on stork nests persisted where platforms were the main

00:04:00.227 --> 00:04:00.847
intervention.

00:04:01.547 --> 00:04:07.067
Heavier nests required more frequent mechanical checks, which raised maintenance costs and storm-related

00:04:07.067 --> 00:04:12.287
faults triggered automatic reclosers that sometimes started small fires and drive vegetation beneath

00:04:12.287 --> 00:04:17.507
the lines. The original decision to treat each pull as an independent nesting site had not

00:04:17.507 --> 00:04:22.447
accounted for the way attractive platforms would cluster activity that had once been dispersed

00:04:22.447 --> 00:04:30.320
across many unsuitable locations. By late 2026, TPAV recommended that insulation, markers, safe

00:04:30.320 --> 00:04:35.840
purchase and platforms be used together rather than platforms alone, and that national risk maps

00:04:35.840 --> 00:04:40.800
incorporate migration routes. Trededash expanded its program to include GPS

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:44.740
tracking of birds and additional conductor covering, reporting no

00:04:44.740 --> 00:04:50.980
electricutions at 46 monitored Imperial Eagle Nests in 2025. ADM electric and

00:04:50.980 --> 00:04:55.740
GDZ electric continued annual platform maintenance and insulation work, now

00:04:55.740 --> 00:04:59.480
framed as part of a broader effort that also addressed climate-driven shifts

00:04:59.480 --> 00:05:04.460
in stork routes. No large-scale removal of platforms has been reported, and

00:05:04.460 --> 00:05:08.760
When operators treat the structures as permanent habitat features that must be managed with

00:05:08.760 --> 00:05:14.415
other engineering controls, decision makers who change only the most visible contact point

00:05:14.415 --> 00:05:19.435
have to model how that change redistributes nests across the rest of the network, not

00:05:19.435 --> 00:05:22.095
only whether deaths at the old contact point decline.

00:05:22.855 --> 00:05:27.035
Fault probability on the pole that becomes the preferred site can rise even when the

00:05:27.035 --> 00:05:28.415
wildlife tally improves.

00:05:29.015 --> 00:05:33.535
Counting saved birds and counting reliable minutes of rural supply are different ledgers

00:05:33.535 --> 00:05:38.235
and a program scored on only one of them can look successful while the other slips.

00:05:38.995 --> 00:05:43.455
Utilities modernizing lines now face that test whenever a retrofit makes one

00:05:43.455 --> 00:05:46.035
structure safer or more attractive than its neighbors.

00:05:46.715 --> 00:05:51.335
In today's grid modernization projects, does the chosen retrofit alter where

00:05:51.335 --> 00:05:56.075
animals or people gather, or does it merely move the original hazard to a new location?

00:05:56.775 --> 00:05:57.975
That's the case for today.

00:05:57.975 --> 00:06:02.135
The lessons tend to travel further when you share them, so send this one to someone

00:06:02.135 --> 00:06:05.135
who'd find it useful, and subscribe wherever you're listening.

00:06:05.515 --> 00:06:06.075
See you tomorrow.

